+| Keep reading | 9/10 | Chapter 8 ending: Seln reports that seven came to drink and “not one of the seven would wet a foot”; Chapter 14 ending: Pike sets an empty tack for the coming hold's slip | Chapters repeatedly resolve one question while opening a sharper one. The stillhound mystery becomes a plan, the plan becomes a costly victory, and the completed job leads to a new job rather than erasing its consequences. | High |
